    "product_id": "6d68fd7e-1dc4-48e5-be19-903441cd9cb0",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 031037\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n237 AM PST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Temperatures will hover within a few degrees of seasonal normals\n  through the week with otherwise quiet conditions.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Monday.\n\nExpect dry conditions, temperatures within a few degrees of seasonal \nnormals, and afternoon breeziness through the work week. Shortwave \nridging will persist across the Desert Southwest for another day \nbefore a weak closed low pushes into the central California Coast \nand across the Great Basin on Wednesday. Impacts from this system \nwill be minimal, with only a slight uptick in wind speeds across the \nforecast area (10 to 20 mph gusts in the afternoon, with gusts to\n25 mph in the higher terrain). Heading into the weekend, heights \nwill increase west-to-east thanks to a high pressure system in the\neastern Pacific Ocean. This will allow temperatures to increase \nto slightly-above normal. In addition to this ridge, a shortwave \nwill pinch off from the upper-level flow and will attempt to close\noff in the southeastern Pacific. The resultant increased pressure\ngradient across our forecast area will increase northerly wind \ngusts Friday and Saturday. In general, wind speeds will remain \nsub-advisory, though speeds will likely approach 40 mph in the \nColorado River Valley as a result of localized topographic \nenhancement. Expect wave heights on Lake Mohave and Lake Havasu to\nexceed 2 feet as a result. \n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast \nPackage...Light winds are expected through the TAF period. Variable \nwinds this morning will become east to northeast after 18Z, but will \nremain under 8 KT. Typical southwest winds this evening will become \nlight and variable again by Wednesday early morning. BKN CIGs around \n20kft will persist through the afternoon then quickly clear after \n00Z.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...In general, light winds \nfollow typical daytime and nighttime patterns are expected across \nthe region through Tuesday early morning. The Owens Valley, \nincluding KBIH, will see breezy south to southeast winds gusting to \naround 20KT become north west between 00Z-03Z, with gusts ending \naround 06Z. KDAG will see increasing west winds this evening around \n06Z with 10-15KT winds gusting to 25KT at times overnight. SCT-BKN \nclouds will continue to stream into the region before clearing late \nthis afternoon and evening from west to east. \n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
